            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_9NYJ9y": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>This season you are invited to join us on a journey through the hills of Mount Kilimanjaro where in the 1960s a Maasai tribesman <em>Ndugu Jumanne Ngoma </em>made a breathtaking discovery. In the heart of the Merelani region in northern Tanzania, glowing blue crystals were found. Initially mistaken for sapphires, the stones were later revealed to be an entirely new gemstone - <strong>tanzanite</strong>.<br/><strong><br/></strong>A couple of decades later, Shamballa Jewels celebrates this magnificent discovery by blending the mysterious tanzanite beads with diamonds and other precious stones and forming a collection like no other. </p>"
          }
        }
      },
